WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.627
File-based secret storage is sometimes unavoidable.

2
00:00:02.627 --> 00:00:08.257
Local agents, appliances, legacy systems, offline tools, and embedded deployments may need secrets on disk.

3
00:00:08.257 --> 00:00:12.385
When that happens, the file becomes part of the security boundary.

4
00:00:12.385 --> 00:00:18.390
It needs a controlled location, strict ownership, narrow permissions, documented platform assumptions, and predictable backup behavior.

5
00:00:18.390 --> 00:00:24.019
A secret file in a convenient shared directory is rarely a good long-term design.

6
00:00:24.019 --> 00:00:29.649
Encryption at rest can help, but it does not solve the whole problem by itself.

7
00:00:29.649 --> 00:00:36.779
If the decryption key is stored next to the encrypted secret, access to one often implies access to both.

8
00:00:36.779 --> 00:00:40.908
Key management, key separation, service identity, and access control remain central.

9
00:00:40.908 --> 00:00:48.789
Teams should also consider backups, deployment artifacts, support bundles, temporary files, and old versions that may preserve secrets long after the

10
00:00:48.789 --> 00:00:50.290
current file is replaced.

11
00:00:50.290 --> 00:00:53.293
C++ file handling should account for platform details.

12
00:00:53.293 --> 00:00:55.920
Permissions can be inherited in surprising ways.

13
00:00:55.920 --> 00:01:00.423
Symlinks or path confusion can undermine assumptions about where data is written.

14
00:01:00.423 --> 00:01:02.675
Temporary files can remain after failure.

15
00:01:02.675 --> 00:01:05.302
Cleanup paths may be skipped during crashes.

16
00:01:05.302 --> 00:01:11.307
Defensive file handling uses controlled directories, explicit permissions, careful error handling, and review of deployment behavior.

17
00:01:11.307 --> 00:01:16.561
When a platform secret store is available, prefer it over inventing a file format.

18
00:01:16.561 --> 00:01:21.440
When files are required, treat them as sensitive operational assets with lifecycle rules.
